## Symptom

IO::K8s::Api::Apiserverinternal::V1alpha1::StorageVersion cannot be inflated at all:

    Cannot locate IO/K8s/Api/Apiserverinternal/V1alpha1/StorageVersionSpec.pm in @INC

StorageVersion.pm:16 declares:

    k8s spec => "Apiserverinternal::V1alpha1::StorageVersionSpec", "required";

The class is not shipped. lib/IO/K8s/Api/Apiserverinternal/V1alpha1/ contains only
ServerStorageVersion.pm, StorageVersion.pm, StorageVersionCondition.pm and
StorageVersionStatus.pm.

Unlike ticket #1, the expansion here is correct: Apiserverinternal is not in
%_class_prefix and the default IO::K8s::Api::$short produces exactly the right
path. The file is simply missing.

## Why this one is unconditional

The attribute is marked "required". The four missing Apiextensions classes only
fail when a CRD happens to use that field; this one fires on every single
StorageVersion, because spec must be present and must be an instance of a class
that does not exist. There is no working path through this class.

That also means it has never worked and is not a regression, so no consumer can
have depended on it.

## Upstream shape

apiserverinternal/v1alpha1.StorageVersionSpec is an empty struct upstream
("StorageVersionSpec is an empty spec"). So the class is trivial: no attributes,
just the package, ABSTRACT, $VERSION and use IO::K8s::Resource. Worth confirming
against the v1.36 spec first, in case a field was added since.

## How it was found

Registry sweep across all shipped modules for unloadable attribute target
classes, alongside ticket #1 and the KubeAggregator expansion bug (ticket #2).

## Suggested direction

Add the class, plus a round-trip test for StorageVersion. An empty spec is
exactly the kind of thing that silently serializes to {} or disappears, so the
test should assert spec survives both directions, not merely that the object
constructs.
